    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n82659" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Περσέπολις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εως</span>,
			ἡ, <u>Persepolis</u>, the ancient
		capital of Persia, and burial place of her kings, <i><span class="en">
			Str.
			15.3.6
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			Arr.
			<u>An.</u>
			7.1.1
		</span></i>. (Shd. perh. be written <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πέρσαι
		πόλις</span> (cf. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πέρσης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					1.1
				</span></i>
			 b); <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Περσαίπολις</span></b>  is
				v.l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				Str.
			</span></i> and written in codd. of <i><span class="en">
				Ael.
				<u>NA</u>
				1.59
			</span></i>.)</div>
